<title>USA: Foodbrands shares up on IBP deal.</title>
<headline>Foodbrands shares up on IBP deal.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Foodbrands America Inc rose 7-3/8 to 23-1/8 after IBP Inc agreed to buy it for $23.40 a share in a transaction valued at $640 million, a deal that analysts said made sense for both firms.</p>
<p>IBP Inc shares were down 3/8 at 24-5/8.</p>
<p>&quot;It looks like a good fit. It should not be dilutive to (IBP's) earnings, even with goodwill that's expected to be about $8.0 million annually,&quot; Prudential analyst John McMillin said.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it's a very good move strategically,&quot; Natwest Securities analyst David Nelson added.</p>
</text>
